Subject: Object creation: extend the inline property-array path to arrays and arguments, and add the `QJS_ALLOC_STATS` measurement build

What this does
  Object creation: extend the inline property-array path to arrays and arguments, and add the `QJS_ALLOC_STATS` measurement build.

Why we need it
  And every array and arguments object paid a second `js_malloc` for its property array even though the object block already reserves room for a small inline property array.

What it adds
  `JS_NewObjectFromShape` adds `JS_CLASS_ARRAY`, `JS_CLASS_ARGUMENTS` and `JS_CLASS_MAPPED_ARGUMENTS` to the classes that embed their property array when `sh->prop_size <= JS_OBJ_INLINE_PROPS`, and a `QJS_ALLOC_STATS` counter block (objects allocated, inline vs separate, property sizes, per-class split, shapes, growth moves/reallocs, GC runs and walked objects, for-in start/next/hasprop) dumped at teardown when the `QJS_ALLOC_STATS` environment variable is set.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
